 to  uh to doxorubicin now of course we can  do a similar thing  using machine learning so what we'll do  now is let's set up  a three class model with  dosatox dosataxel doxorubicin  and the negative controls and now  this let's do the same thing let's look  for things that are similar to jackson  rubison  and see if we get something similar  so here's our model we can see the  accuracy is 95 percent  and then down here we see the results of  it here of course doxorubicin is high  and then again we can see for the colon  bleomice and our various dna damaging  agents popping up  so i think this gives you a very nice  example of  how easy it is to run the analysis in  strata miner  and how you can easily handle larger  numbers of features  and then move back and forth in the  workflow to get the most information  the most possible knowledge out of your  data  this approach of generating as many  measurements as you can and having easy  access to advanced methods to mine them  gives one major benefit if you're simply  extracting a single measurement from an  experiment  you have to iterate over experiments in  order to generate new knowledge  with the types of biological systems  that are commonly used now  3d models patient drive cell lines this  can get very  very expensive  within carta and stratiminer however you  can iterate over the analysis  measure everything that you can at high  resolution  and then you can ask multiple questions  of the data set  strata mining makes this very easy  because you can easily jump back and  forth within the workflow  new information generated can be merged  as new metadata  to enrich the analysis  you can also use the information to  rapidly refine your image analysis  this is especially valuable in the assay  development and piloting  stages if you'd like to know more about  the stratominer platform you go to our  website  or if you contact us at one of these  emails we'll get back to you  with that i'd like to thank you all fo